{#
  The version links to its release notes on GitHub.

  Two things make that link safe to have. The repository URL comes from
  site.json, so it is declared once with the rest of the global metadata rather
  than hardcoded here. And the link checker excludes this repository's
  releases/tag/ URLs, because in a release pull request version.txt already
  holds the NEW version while its tag does not exist yet -- without the
  exclusion the link would be a guaranteed 404 on exactly the pull request that
  bumps it, the same trap the changelog's compare link set.

  The version is spelled out rather than rendered as a bare "v1.0.1", so it
  needs no visually-hidden label and no ARIA: "Version 1.0.1" reads correctly
  aloud and on screen, and works as link text that describes where it goes.
#}
<footer class="site-footer">
  <p class="footer-text">&copy; {{ build.year }} {{ site.author }}. All rights reserved.</p>
  <p class="footer-version">
    <a href="{{ site.repository }}/releases/tag/v{{ build.version }}">Version {{ build.version }}</a>
  </p>
</footer>
